<!--
  Hand-written test fixture for Novox's MusicXML importer (MIT, like the engine). It is laid out
  the way MuseScore Studio 4.7 exports a song: the piano part listed before the voice, tempo text
  (metronome plus <sound tempo> rounded to two decimals) only in the top part, a pickup measure
  numbered "0" with implicit="yes", chords written lowest note first with the lyric on that
  note, <lyric number="verse + 1"> with syllabic/text/extend, an elision typed inside one <text>,
  a cue note, <forward> for a voice that starts late, and endings with a backward repeat in
  every part.

  Played out: pickup, m1-m3 (verse 1, first ending), m1-m2 (verse 2), m4 (second ending), m5.
-->
